Ok, so I guess I said that wrong. I guess I should have said that the
shovel or pickaxe should not be considered a weapon if wielded, just as
lamps and wands can be wielded, but do not break weaponless conduct.

I don't expect the properties of the pickaxe to be changed. That's why I
proposed the shovel as a pure tool: one which is not wielded by applying
it, or if wielded is not treated as a weapon in combat. (Wielding a lamp
or a magic marker is just like striking bare-handed, right?)

The way things work now, btw, exchanging with nothing or unwielding a tool
gives the opposing monster a free strike. Maybe that's something that
could be changed as well: going to empty-handed could not take a turn.

